<!-- formalization -->

**Definition (`InfoSys.directedSup`).** The directed supremum of a nonempty directed family is the family supremum of that family, available because directedness yields finite consistency of the union carrier.

**Theorem (`InfoSys.directedSup.carrier_eq_union`).** The carrier of a directed supremum equals the family-union carrier.

*Proof.* Deductive closure always enlarges the union; the reverse uses that finite antecedents in the union sit in a single member, which is already deductively closed. □

**Theorem (`InfoSys.directedSup.le`).** If every member of the family approximates an upper bound, then the directed supremum approximates that bound.

*Proof.* This is the corresponding property of the family supremum. □

**Theorem (`InfoSys.directedSup.le_of_mem`).** Every member of the family approximates the directed supremum.

*Proof.* This is the corresponding property of the family supremum. □

**Theorem (`InfoSys.directedSup.compact_closure`).** If a finitely generated element approximates a directed supremum, then it approximates some member of the family.

*Proof.* The generators lie in the union carrier, hence in some member by directedness; that member’s deductive closure then dominates the finite element. □
